Generate 0039-lus-frameinterp-path-underflow-guard.patch.

Fix the device crash: `signal 11` in Object_DrawAll on Corneria boss death
(all-range mode). The fault return address (Object_DrawAll + 264) sits right
after `bl _FrameInterpolation_RecordOpenChild`, whose first act is
`current_path.back()` — a deref that is UB (segfault) when current_path is
empty.

Root cause: `is_recording` can toggle MID-FRAME —
FrameInterpolation_ShouldInterpolateFrame() sets it directly, and StartRecord
leaves it false at the 20 fps interpolation bucket (the boss-death slowdown
can dip there). Both RecordOpenChild and RecordCloseChild early-return when
!is_recording, so if recording flips between a matched Open and Close, the
push/pop go unbalanced. An extra Close then pops the ROOT path off
current_path, leaving it empty, and the next RecordOpenChild/append derefs
current_path.back() on an empty vector -> crash. The boss-death frame (many
scenery360/actor/effect draws in the all-range branch) is where the imbalance
surfaces.

Fix (pristine LUS/port code, robustness only):
- RecordCloseChild: NEVER pop the root. `if (current_path.size() <= 1)
  return;` before the pop. The root must always remain (StartRecord relies on
  it). Popping it is always a bug regardless of the imbalance source. Counts
  the guard hits into gSoh3DDbgInterpGuard (bridge `3d`) so the fix can be
  confirmed to have engaged on-device.
- RecordOpenChild: belt-and-suspenders empty-check before the .back() deref.

__IOS__-guards only the telemetry counter (defined in the shell); the guards
themselves are unconditional so the macOS build gets the same safety.


--- a/src/port/interpolation/FrameInterpolation.cpp
+++ b/src/port/interpolation/FrameInterpolation.cpp
@@ -442,6 +442,10 @@
 
 void FrameInterpolation_RecordOpenChild(const void* a, int b) {
     if (!is_recording)
+        return;
+    // SOH_IOS (overlay 0039): defensive — never deref .back() on an empty
+    // current_path (see the pop guard in RecordCloseChild).
+    if (current_path.empty())
         return;
     label key = { a, b };
     auto& m = current_path.back()->children[key];
@@ -451,7 +455,19 @@
 
 void FrameInterpolation_RecordCloseChild(void) {
     if (!is_recording)
+        return;
+    // SOH_IOS (overlay 0039): NEVER pop the root. is_recording can toggle
+    // mid-frame, so an unbalanced Close would otherwise empty current_path and
+    // the next RecordOpenChild/append would deref .back() on an empty vector =
+    // signal 11 in Object_DrawAll (device: Corneria boss death). Guard hits are
+    // counted so the fix can be confirmed engaged over the `3d` bridge.
+    if (current_path.size() <= 1) {
+#ifdef __IOS__
+        extern volatile int gSoh3DDbgInterpGuard;
+        gSoh3DDbgInterpGuard = gSoh3DDbgInterpGuard + 1;
+#endif
         return;
+    }
     // append(Op::CloseChild);
     if (has_inv_actor_mtx && current_path.size() == inv_actor_mtx_path_index) {
         has_inv_actor_mtx = false;
